## ⭐ If you only have tonight  
Don't read all 20.  
I'd do these **in this exact order**:  
**1.** Anthropic — Building Effective Agents **2.** OpenAI — Practical Guide to Building Agents **3.** Anthropic — Writing Effective Tools **4.** Anthropic — Demystifying Evals **5.** LangChain — Agent Evals **6.** ReliabilityBench **7.** ReAct **8.** Reflexion  
Then use the benchmarks to get ideas for **how to test your own system**, rather than trying to implement the benchmarks themselves.  
For your hackathon, the biggest takeaway to keep in your head is:  
**Don't make the agent look complicated. Make it measurable, recoverable, observable, and demonstrably better.**  
